Context()->texStrings;
BEGIN_TEXT
Let \( R \) be the pentagon with vertices \( (1,0),(3,0),(4,2),(2,3) \) and \( (0,2) \). Let \( C_1 \) and \( C_2 \) be two oriented curves starting at \( (1,0) \) and ending at \( (3,0) \) as shown below. $BR

\{ image( "k3-q7-pentagon.png", width=>260, height=>234) \}
$BR
Computing \( I  = \int_{C_2} (F\cdot n) ds \) by direct parameterization is a long mess. Do not attempt this approach.  Instead, compute \( I \) by moving the line integral to \( C_1 \).
 $BR

\{$q1->ans_rule\}




END_TEXT
Context()->normalStrings;

##############################################################
#
#  Answers
#
#

ANS($q1->with(tolerance=>.01)->cmp);


# default tolerance is .01 or one percent.


